# Allow-list context for `jellyfin-plugin/Dockerfile` (build context is src/, and
# Docker prefers this file over src/.dockerignore).
#
# The last matching pattern wins, so the shape is: take everything away, then put
# back exactly what the image needs. src/core has NO rule at all here - the
# library travels inside the plugin DLL (the csproj embeds only ../core/*.py
# through the read-only /core mount of plugin-build, a different build), so
# src/core/thabit_translator.conf with its real OpenSubtitles/SubDL credentials
# never even enters this context.
*
!jellyfin-plugin/
jellyfin-plugin/**
!jellyfin-plugin/docker/
jellyfin-plugin/docker/**
!jellyfin-plugin/docker/*.sh
!jellyfin-plugin/Dockerfile
!jellyfin-plugin/Dockerfile.dockerignore
!jellyfin-plugin/artifacts/
jellyfin-plugin/artifacts/**
!jellyfin-plugin/artifacts/*.zip

# Explicit deny (belt and braces): should anyone ever add a rule for core/ above,
# the credentials file stays out.
core/thabit_translator.conf
core/**/thabit_translator.conf
